ld create another Pung, but the remaining tiles (W8, T3, T8, B6, F3, J1, J2, J3) lack the necessary combinations to form a winning hand. Passing allows flexibility to draw or wait for more viable tiles.\nReason: Penging T5 would not contribute to a valid winning hand structure due to insufficient meld/pair potential in remaining tiles. Passing preserves options for future draws or discards.\nAnswer: Pass"}
